      "title": "PHAR2001_3_1_3_ADH_water_saver",
      "library": "H5P.QuestionSet 1.21",
      "params": {
        "introPage": {
          "showIntroPage": false,
          "startButtonText": "Start Quiz",
          "introduction": ""
        },
        "progressType": "dots",
        "passPercentage": 50,
        "questions": [
          {
            "params": {
              "media": {
                "disableImageZooming": false
              },
              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>ADH is antidiuretic hormone, the water saver.</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>When you awaken from a night where you drank too much ethanol (the alchol in beverages) the decreased circulating ADH contributes to the hangover, and is the reason your tongue is stuck to the roof of your mouth.</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Some drugs affect ADH secretion or actions, and as such may result in inadvertent diuretic or antidiuretic effects.</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Desmopressin is the treatment of ADH insufficiency.</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No, ADH is secreted from the posterior pituitary, which is the side that only has two hormones, ADH and Oxytocin. Those two hormones are very similar.</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Indeed, ADH is secreted from the <strong>posterior pituitary,</strong> which is the side that only has two hormones, ADH and Oxytocin. Those two hormones are very similar.</div>\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>ADH is secreted from the anterior pituitary gland</div>\n"
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
